mixin () {
  /// Returns the backend API documentation as static Markdown.
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# Finance Tracker Backend API\n\nBackend for a personal finance tracker. Each caller owns a private set of\nmovements (income and expenses) and can read aggregated summaries and\nper-category expense totals over a selectable period.\n\n## Authentication and authorization\n\n- Every method below is **per-caller**: data is stored under the caller's\n  principal and only that principal can read or mutate its own movements.\n- `addTransaction`, `updateTransaction` and `deleteTransaction` are update\n  calls and require a signed (non-anonymous) caller. An anonymous caller gets\n  its own empty, isolated store.\n- `listTransactions`, `getSummary` and `getCategoryTotals` are query calls and\n  also scope their result to the caller.\n- The app's frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at\n  `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available. An agent already holding\n  the user's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app\n  principal against that origin (for example\n  `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). Such a delegation acts with the\n  user's full authority in this app until it expires.\n- Registration is not required to call these methods: the first call from a\n  principal simply creates its own empty store. A principal that never signed\n  in through the app's frontend is a different principal than the one the\n  frontend registered, so it sees an empty store.\n\n## Units and encodings\n\n- `amount` is a whole, positive currency unit count (`Nat`). Zero is rejected\n  with `#invalidAmount`.\n- `date` is a `Timestamp`: milliseconds since the Unix epoch (`Nat`).\n- `txType` is the variant `{ #income; #expense }`.\n- `category` is the variant\n  `{ #food; #transport; #entertainment; #home; #health; #other }`.\n- `note` is an optional `Text` (`?Text`); pass `null` for no note.\n- `id` is a `Nat` assigned by the backend, unique per caller.\n- `Period` is the variant `{ #currentMonth; #previousMonth; #all }`. Month\n  boundaries are computed in UTC.\n\n## Methods\n\n### addTransaction(input : TransactionInput) : Result<Transaction, FinanceError>\n\nRegisters a new movement for the caller and returns the stored transaction\nwith its assigned `id`. Fails with `#invalidAmount` when `amount` is zero.\n\n### updateTransaction(id : TransactionId, input : TransactionInput) : Result<Transaction, FinanceError>\n\nReplaces an existing movement owned by the caller. Fails with `#notFound(id)`\nwhen the caller has no movement with that id, or `#invalidAmount` when `amount`\nis zero.\n\n### deleteTransaction(id : TransactionId) : Result<(), FinanceError>\n\nRemoves a movement owned by the caller. Fails with `#notFound(id)` when the\ncaller has no movement with that id.\n\n### listTransactions(period : Period, txType : ?TxType) : [Transaction]\n\nReturns the caller's movements matching `period`, newest first (ties broken by\ndescending id). Pass `null` for `txType` to include both income and expenses.\n\n### getSummary(period : Period) : Summary\n\nReturns `{ balance; totalIncome; totalExpense; transactionCount }` for the\ncaller over `period`. `balance` is `totalIncome - totalExpense` as an `Int`\n(it may be negative).\n\n### getCategoryTotals(period : Period) : [CategoryTotal]\n\nReturns one entry per category in display order\n(food, transport, entertainment, home, health, other), each with the\naccumulated **expense** total, its `percentage` of total expense (integer,\n0-100), and `isTop` marking the category with the highest expense. Categories\nwith no expense report `total = 0`, `percentage = 0`, `isTop = false`.\n\n## Lifecycle and polling\n\nAll methods are single-call and return their result immediately; there is no\nasynchronous job to poll.\n\n## Mutation retry safety\n\n- `addTransaction` is **not idempotent**: each successful call creates a new\n  movement with a fresh id. Retrying a call that already succeeded creates a\n  duplicate.\n- `updateTransaction` and `deleteTransaction` are idempotent in effect for a\n  given id: re-applying an update yields the same state, and a second delete\n  returns `#notFound(id)`.\n- `deleteTransaction` is destructive and cannot be undone.\n\n## Errors and limits\n\n- `FinanceError` is `{ #invalidAmount; #notFound : TransactionId; #notAuthorized }`.\n  `#notAuthorized` is reserved and not currently produced by these methods.\n- Amounts are `Nat`; there is no upper bound enforced beyond the platform's\n  numeric limits.\n- `getApiDoc` is a query method returning this static document.\n";
  };
};
